[# flows/welcome: the welcome flow, written with the welcome recipe.

   The recipe supplies the structure (preheader, header, hero, footer), and the data here supplies the content. Only the
   hero is filled in, since the rest of a welcome email needs real brand copy, products and reviews. Add sections as the
   brand has them: brandIntro, benefits, bestSellers, socialProof and cta (see docs/recipes.md). Brand values come from the
   tokens (t.*) so this builds for any brand. #]
[% extends "layouts/base.mjml" %]

[% block body %]
[[ recipe('welcome', {
  hero: {
    eyebrow: 'Welcome, ' + v('customer.first_name'),
    headline: 'Welcome to ' + t.brand.name,
    description: 'Thanks for joining us. Here is what happens next.',
    cta: { label: 'Start exploring', href: v('brand.url') },
    image: { src: t.images.hero, alt: 'Welcome to ' + t.brand.name }
  }
}) ]]
[% endblock %]
